WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.644 --> 00:00:02.609
(light upbeat music)

00:00:02.609 --> 00:00:05.198
- [Dan] It's like a
symphony of manipulating

00:00:05.198 --> 00:00:09.365
and spinning and flipping
the cards in your hands.

00:00:09.867 --> 00:00:11.672
It's like each move inspires the next

00:00:11.672 --> 00:00:15.378
and you're not even thinking about it.

00:00:15.378 --> 00:00:18.947
The cards are dancing between the hands,

00:00:18.947 --> 00:00:21.178
they're spinning around,
they're flipping over,

00:00:21.178 --> 00:00:22.203
they're doing things

00:00:22.203 --> 00:00:25.487
you wouldn't even expect them to be doing.

00:00:25.487 --> 00:00:27.382
(light upbeat music)

00:00:27.382 --> 00:00:31.092
It's just so surprising, almost magical.

00:00:31.092 --> 00:00:34.342
(light dramatic music)

00:00:37.008 --> 00:00:40.091
(light upbeat music)

00:00:41.003 --> 00:00:42.298
For as long as I can remember

00:00:42.298 --> 00:00:46.465
we've always done things
in tandem together.

00:00:46.694 --> 00:00:50.223
We both got into magic
around the age of 12,

00:00:50.223 --> 00:00:52.740
we would go to the library
and check out books

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:55.229
by Dai Vernon, Guy Hollingworth,

00:00:55.229 --> 00:00:56.885
just seeing the illustrations were like,

00:00:56.885 --> 00:01:00.255
wow, we can do this with playing cards?

00:01:00.255 --> 00:01:04.422
When we started practicing
cardistry, it wasn't a thing,

00:01:05.199 --> 00:01:09.223
it has its roots in magic,
it comes from card magicians,

00:01:09.223 --> 00:01:11.694
who would use what is
called a card flourish

00:01:11.694 --> 00:01:14.664
and these were used to accentuate

00:01:14.664 --> 00:01:17.496
certain moments in a magic trick,

00:01:17.496 --> 00:01:20.364
so we took that and just ran with it.

00:01:20.364 --> 00:01:24.531
We were the first to embrace
it and really focus on it

00:01:24.704 --> 00:01:26.752
and practice it as its own thing

00:01:26.752 --> 00:01:29.419
and promote it as its own thing.

00:01:31.139 --> 00:01:34.306
(light dynamic music)

00:01:35.664 --> 00:01:37.616
Cardistry is very much like skateboarding,

00:01:37.616 --> 00:01:39.246
you know, we practice these tricks

00:01:39.246 --> 00:01:41.667
until we have them down perfect, you know,

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:45.046
we see other tricks and we're
like, oh, we gotta learn that,

00:01:45.046 --> 00:01:46.837
you know, 52 playing cards

00:01:46.837 --> 00:01:51.004
and the possibilities to maneuver
those around are endless.

00:01:51.509 --> 00:01:53.441
You can hold a deck of cards in your hand

00:01:53.441 --> 00:01:55.332
and it's one solid block,

00:01:55.332 --> 00:01:57.621
now imagine lifting up another block,

00:01:57.621 --> 00:01:58.970
so now you have two,

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:02.225
well, what can you do with
those two blocks in your hands?

00:02:02.225 --> 00:02:05.221
Well, you can create more
blocks and we call those packets

00:02:05.221 --> 00:02:07.313
and you can start maneuvering and spinning

00:02:07.313 --> 00:02:11.105
and flipping those packets
between your fingers.

00:02:11.105 --> 00:02:14.772
It's hard, like it takes
a lot of dexterity,

00:02:16.373 --> 00:02:19.245
it's all practiced, it's all rehearsed

00:02:19.245 --> 00:02:20.977
and when you're truly a master,

00:02:20.977 --> 00:02:22.706
you can just start doing things on the fly

00:02:22.706 --> 00:02:26.515
and you don't even have to think about it.

00:02:26.515 --> 00:02:29.598
(light upbeat music)

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:37.957
What kids are doing today
with cards is mind blowing,

00:02:38.249 --> 00:02:40.741
if you would have told me
that when I was 14 years old,

00:02:40.741 --> 00:02:44.234
I would have been like,
that's the coolest thing,

00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:47.516
I had no idea that it
could even be this big.

00:02:47.516 --> 00:02:49.256
The ultimate goal would be

00:02:49.256 --> 00:02:52.554
to get people to almost
put cardistry first,

00:02:52.554 --> 00:02:53.917
when they see a deck of playing cards,

00:02:53.917 --> 00:02:55.687
you know, it's no longer for games,

00:02:55.687 --> 00:02:59.354
it's no longer for
gambling, it's cardistry.

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:03.733
(light upbeat music)

